FFCS Simulator and Analysis GUI
A MATLAB-based graphical application for simulating and analysing Fluorescence Fluctuation Correlation Spectroscopy (FFCS) datasets, including:

FCS (Fluorescence Correlation Spectroscopy)
ICS (Image Correlation Spectroscopy)
TICS (Temporal Image Correlation Spectroscopy)
STICS (Spatio-Temporal Image Correlation Spectroscopy)
Developed as a training and teaching tool to help users understand how molecular diffusion, flow, concentration, noise, bleaching, and molecular brightness influence fluorescence correlation analyses.

Features
Simulate fluorescence image time series and FCS traces
Configure diffusion, flow, particle density and molecular brightness
Add detector noise, background noise and photobleaching
Analyse simulated data using FCS, ICS, TICS and STICS
Compare recovered parameters with known simulation inputs
Ideal for workshops, teaching and method development
Installation
Download the appropriate release for your operating system.
Run the installer located in the Distribution folder.
Install the required MATLAB Runtime if prompted.
Launch the GUI from the desktop shortcut.
Requirements
MATLAB Runtime R2024b (Windows) or R2025b (macOS)
~3.5 GB free disk space
Sufficient RAM for large image-series datasets
MATLAB Runtime can be downloaded from:

https://au.mathworks.com/products/compiler/matlab-runtime.html

Basic Workflow
Initialise Parameters
Configure simulation settings
Define particle population properties
Generate simulated FFCS data
Select an analysis method (FCS, ICS, TICS or STICS)
Compute correlation functions
Fit the selected model and recover parameters
Educational Objectives
The software provides a hands-on environment for learning:

Molecular diffusion measurements
Directed flow analysis
Number density estimation
Correlation function interpretation
Effects of noise and bleaching on FFCS experiments
Because the ground-truth simulation parameters are known, users can directly evaluate the accuracy and limitations of different analysis approaches.

Citation
If you use this software for teaching or research, please cite:

Pandzic E, Whan RM. A Practical Guide to Fluorescence Temporal and Spatial Correlation Spectroscopy. The Biophysicist. 2021;2(1):40–69. DOI: 10.35459/tbp.2019.000143

